## Two tooling defects — proved pre-existing against untouched backups, not patched

- `_verify_payslip.py` raises `NameError: IFERROR` and cannot complete (identical on the backup)
- `verify_specs.py` C6 demands the phrase "does not exist" in Version Control — correct pre-Stage-4, stale now; it produces 8 of the 11 errors

Patching a checker in the same pass as the artifacts it checks would destroy the only independent signal that the pass was clean.

